"metadata", "contents": [{"content": "All's Well That Ends Well", "type": "lesson_name"}, {"content": "Words of Encouragement", "type": "unit_name"}, {"content": 3, "type": "position"}, {"content": "stub", "type": "origin"}, {"content": 16, "type": "lesson"}, {"content": "B2.3", "type": "level"}]}, {"type": "achievment_test", "contents": [{"content": "false", "type": "test"}]}, {"type": "objectives", "contents": [{"content": "Exchange information about unlikely events or fairly certain conditions that will be fulfilled in present, past or future  in spoken or written texts and in work and social contexts.", "type": "primary"}, {"content": "Understands extended speeches, lectures, articles and reports of the professional, academic, or daily life on a wide range of general and work topics, in conversations or presentations, spoken at a natural speed and in circumstances that make it more difficult to hear.", "type": "secondary_1"}, {"content": "Understands extended speeches, lectures, articles and reports of the professional, academic, or daily life on a wide range of general and work topics, in conversations or presentations, spoken at a natural speed and in circumstances that make it more difficult to hear.", "type": "secondary_2"}, {"content": "Understands extended speeches, lectures, articles and reports of the professional, academic, or daily life on a wide range of general and work topics, in conversations or presentations, spoken at a natural speed and in circumstances that make it more difficult to hear.", "type": "secondary_3"}, {"content": "Understands extended speeches, lectures, articles and reports of the professional, academic, or daily life on a wide range of general and work topics, in conversations or presentations, spoken at a natural speed and in circumstances that make it more difficult to hear.", "type": "secondary_4"}, {"content": "Understands extended speeches, lectures, articles and reports of the professional, academic, or daily life on a wide range of general and work topics, in conversations or presentations, spoken at a natural speed and in circumstances that make it more difficult to hear.", "type": "secondary_5"}, {"content": "Understands extended speeches, lectures, articles and reports of the professional, academic, or daily life on a wide range of general and work topics, in conversations or presentations, spoken at a natural speed and in circumstances that make it more difficult to hear.", "type": "secondary_6"}, {"content": "Understands extended speeches, lectures, articles and reports of the professional, academic, or daily life on a wide range of general and work topics, in conversations or presentations, spoken at a natural speed and in circumstances that make it more difficult to hear.", "type": "secondary_7"}, {"content": "Understands extended speeches, lectures, articles and reports of the professional, academic, or daily life on a wide range of general and work topics, in conversations or presentations, spoken at a natural speed and in circumstances that make it more difficult to hear.", "type": "secondary_8"}]}, {"content": "engenn11le16ob03re1img01.jpg", "type": "background_image"}, {"type": "learning_points", "contents": [{"content": "Meaning of Perfect Modals ", "type": "heading"}, {"content": "Perfect modals can have different meanings than their present counterparts. You use the structure modal + have + past participle to make sentences with perfect modals.", "type": "describer"}, {"content": "<span class = \"strong\">Could have </span>- to talk about unrealistic past possibilities (you use this structure with the third conditional)  </br>For example: </br><span class=\"italic\">I <span class=\"strong\">could have gone</span> away for vacation, but decided to have a staycation instead.</span>", "type": "text"}, {"content": "<span class = \"strong\">Will have</span> - to talk about something that will happen before another action in the future. It can also show that something will occur before a specific time in the future.  </br>For example:</br><span class=\"italic\">I <span class = \"strong\">will have completed </span>the project before you return from holidays.</span></br><span class=\"italic\">  I <span class=\"strong\">will have gone</span> away for vacation this time next week.</span>", "type": "text"}, {"content": "<span class = \"strong\">May/might have</span> - to talk about realistic past possibilities </br>For example: </br> <span class=\"italic\">I <span class=\"strong\">might have seen</span> you at the mall the other day, I just can't be sure. </span>", "type": "text"}, {"content": "<span class = \"strong\">Should have</span> - to express regrets </br> For example: </br><span class=\"italic\">I <span class=\"strong\">shouldn't have eaten</span> so much pizza - I feel sick now!</span>", "type": "text"}, {"content": "<span class = \"strong\">Must have</span> - to make logical deductions  </br>For example: </br> <span class=\"italic\">That car is gorgeous - it <span class=\"strong\">must have cost</span> you a pretty penny! </span>", "type": "text"}, {"content": "You <span class = \"strong\">may have</span> worked here a long time, but tonight I witnessed you disparage and belittle colleagues in front of customers.", "type": "example"}, {"content": "You <span class = \"strong\">may have</span> done a good job in the past,  but I have recently seen you mistreat customers.", "type": "example"}, {"content": "Jose <span class = \"strong\">might have</span> opened the till.", "type": "example"}, {"content": "The other bartender <span class = \"strong\">might have</span> done it.", "type": "example"}]}, {"type": "learning_points", "contents": [{"content": "The Comparative Clause: Manner", "type": "heading"}, {"content": "You can use adverbial clauses of comparison to describe manner (the way in which someone does something).", "type": "describer"}, {"content": "Using comparative clauses helps to make your language use more descriptive and dynamic. ", "type": "text"}, {"content": "You introduce the comparative clause with the relative adverb <span class=\"italic\">as</span>.", "type": "text"}, {"content": "For example:", "type": "text"}, {"content": "<span class=\"italic\">You may do <span class=\"strong\">as you wish.</span></br> It ended <span class=\"strong\">as I expected it would.</span> ", "type": "text"}, {"content": "When<span class=\"italic\"> as</span> comes at the beginning of the sentence, it can sound quite formal and old-fashioned.</br>For example:</br><span class = \"italic\"><span class = \"strong\">As</span> you are aware, the project needs to be finalized by Tuesday.</br></span><span class = \"italic\"><span class = \"strong\">As</span> we all know, the company is moving ahead with the expansion.</span>", "type": "text"}, {"content": "Take a look at some other examples from the text:", "type": "text"}, {"content": "I've been working as hard as anyone here. ", "type": "example"}, {"content": "Who works as hard as me?", "type": "example"}, {"content": " I am not as silly as you think! ", "type": "example"}, {"content": "You are speaking as if you are the manager.", "type": "example"}, {"content": "I do the work as it should be done.", "type": "example"}]}, {"type": "target_word", "contents": [{"content": "job performance", "type": "name"}, {"content": "ability to carry out or accomplish an action, task, or function at work", "type": "definition"}, {"content": "(noun)", "type": "part_speech"}, {"content": "Example: We need to talk about your job performance.", "type": "example"}, {"content": "engenn11le16ob03aud01", "type": "audio"}]}, {"type": "target_word_describer", "contents": [{"content": "These are words you use when you are a manager.", "type": "text"}]}, {"type": "target_word", "contents": [{"content": "disposition", "type": "name"}, {"content": "a person's inherent qualities of mind and character", "type": "definition"}, {"content": "(noun)", "type": "part_speech"}, {"content": "Example: Your disposition lately has been surly at best.", "type": "example"}, {"content": "engenn11le16ob03aud02", "type": "audio"}]}, {"type": "target_word", "contents": [{"content": "surly", "type": "name"}, {"content": "bad-tempered and unfriendly", "type": "definition"}, {"content": "(adjective)", "type": "part_speech"}, {"content": "Example: My grandpa can be very surly when he isn't feeling well.", "type": "example"}, {"content": "engenn11le16ob03aud03", "type": "audio"}]}, {"type": "target_word", "contents": [{"content": "problematic", "type": "name"}, {"content": "presenting a problem or difficulty", "type": "definition"}, {"content": "(adjective)", "type": "part_speech"}, {"content": "Example: Your demeanor towards customers and co-workers has become problematic.", "type": "example"}, {"content": "engenn11le16ob03aud04", "type": "audio"}]}, {"type": "target_word", "contents": [{"content": "besides the point", "type": "name"}, {"content": "not important or relevant", "type": "definition"}, {"content": "(expression)", "type": "part_speech"}, {"content": "Example: That's besides the point.", "type": "example"}, {"content": "engenn11le16ob03aud05", "type": "audio"}]}, {"type": "target_word", "contents": [{"content": "to disparage", "type": "name"}, {"content": "to regard or represent as being of little worth", "type": "definition"}, {"content": "(verb)", "type": "part_speech"}, {"content": "Example: I witnessed you disparage colleagues in front of customers.", "type": "example"}, {"content": "engenn11le16ob03aud06", "type": "audio"}]}, {"type": "target_word", "contents": [{"content": "to belittle", "type": "name"}, {"content": " to make someone or something seem unimportant", "type": "definition"}, {"content": "(verb)", "type": "part_speech"}, {"content": "Example:  I witnessed you belittle colleagues in front of customers.", "type": "example"}, {"content": "engenn11le16ob03aud07", "type": "audio"}]}, {"type": "target_word", "contents": [{"content": "wicked", "type": "name"}, {"content": " evil or morally wrong", "type": "definition"}, {"content": "(adjective)", "type": "part_speech"}, {"content": "Example: Nothing is permanent in this wicked world.", "type": "example"}, {"content": "engenn11le16ob03aud08", "type": "audio"}]}, {"type": "takeaway_assessment", "contents": [{"content": "I discuss what type of management would be interesting to me.", "type": "text"}, {"content": "I brainstorm what skills a manager needs.", "type": "text"}, {"content": "I brainstorm the pros and cons of the job.", "type": "text"}, {"content": "I describe in writing why I would or wouldn't like to be a manager explaining why.", "type": "text"}, {"content": "I give feedback to my partner.", "type": "text"}]}, {"type": "takeaway_extension", "contents": [{"content": "With a partner, discuss what kind of management you think it would be good to get into \u2013 hotel management, sports, entertainment, tourism, business ... ?", "type": "text"}, {"content": "What skills does a manager need to have?", "type": "text"}, {"content": "Make a list of the pros and cons of being a manager.", "type": "text"}, {"content": "Write 200 words describing why you would like to be a manager or why you wouldn't. Explain your reasons.", "type": "text"}, {"content": "Have a partner read your writing and give feedback.", "type": "text"}]}]}